<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Himayat Sagar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1927</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Himayat Sagar is a reservoir on the Esi river near Hyderabad, completed in 1927 under the Nizam Osman Ali Khan and named after his son Azam Jah, Himayat Ali Khan. With the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-sagar">Osman Sagar</a>, it was built after the disastrous Musi flood of 1908 to protect the city from floods and supply it with drinking water.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/himayat-sagar.jpg" alt="Himayat Sagar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Randhirreddy · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Himayat_Sagar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
